{
  "file": "first-100-ukrainian-words.pdf",
  "title": "Your first 100 Ukrainian words",
  "subtitle": "A printable starter kit from a native Ukrainian tutor — with pronunciation",
  "intro": [
    "These are the words I would teach you in your first weeks: the ones you need to greet people, ask simple questions, order a coffee and find your way. Learn them in small groups, say each one out loud, and you will already be able to hold a tiny conversation.",
    "The stressed vowel is shown in colour in the Ukrainian (дя́кую) and the stressed syllable is written in capitals in the pronunciation (DYA-ku-yu). Stress in Ukrainian is free, so learn it together with the word — it is the quickest way to sound natural."
  ],
  "labels": {
    "a": "Ukrainian",
    "tr": "Say it",
    "b": "English"
  },
  "sections": [
    {
      "h2": "Greetings and politeness",
      "intro": "The words you will use in every single conversation.",
      "items": [
        {
          "a": "приві́т",
          "tr": "pry-VIT",
          "b": "hi",
          "note": "informal"
        },
        {
          "a": "до́брий день",
          "tr": "DOB-ryi den",
          "b": "hello, good afternoon",
          "note": "polite, any time of day"
        },
        {
